# Build-context ignore for infra/Dockerfile.
# BuildKit reads "<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore" in preference to a context
# root .dockerignore, so this scopes cleanly to the production build.
#
# Defense-in-depth: the Dockerfile already COPYs selectively (it never does
# `COPY . .` and never touches infra/), but this keeps host secrets, local
# caches, and build outputs out of the build context entirely.

# Secrets and local env — never shipped into an image.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Installed deps and build outputs — the image installs and builds fresh.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo

# VCS, logs, coverage/report artifacts, and the derived knowledge graph.
.git
.github
**/*.log
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
graphify-out

# Infra runtime material (nginx/postgres/redis configs, TLS certs, env
# examples) is mounted at run time, not baked into the image.
infra
